  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two doors, one contract",
      "items": [
        "webui_report (in-process, registered beside webui_present) and POST /api/report (localhost agent surface) emit byte-identical frames through the shared report-frame builder; exact-one-body-mode validation; 16MB cap.",
        "The Report tab is the ONLY render surface: markdown renders DOM-built (no HTML parsing of producer content); html renders in a sandboxed iframe (allow-scripts allow-downloads) at 70vh with fullscreen + open-standalone hatches.",
        "The standalone door GET /api/report/<id>/raw serves an html frame as a top-level page (same CSP as /files) — the true separate-page case for sharing/export."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "BTW — the ask direction reversed",
      "items": [
        "ask cards flow agent -> webui (HITL inbox); BTW branches flow webui -> agent: the user authors a question seeded with report context, the agent answers in chat.",
        "Loop closure: queuing fires onBtwCreate -> the bound TUI session is belled instantly (no polling); the tab badges pending from ANY pane (15s visibility-gated poll; 4s detail poll on-pane).",
        "The event mirror btw-<port>.jsonl (create/resolve lines, best-effort, same contract as report persistence) survives restarts; the agent drains via webui {mode:'btw'} (pure fetch, no browser) and resolves each id."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Cleanup is total; restarts stay clean",
      "items": [
        "DELETE /api/report/<id> removes the frame from the live store AND compacts the mirror (order preserved, corrupt lines kept); unknown ids 404. DELETE /api/report clears all and returns {removed:n}.",
        "Shell affordances: a x button on EVERY report article (markdown too) and a pane-level clear-all toolbar that appears with articles and self-removes when empty; other open tabs catch up on refresh (connect-time snapshot is the source of truth).",
        "The mirror was append-only by design (it WAS the archive); cleanup compacts it — measured: restore of 25 archify-class frames (~16MB mirror) parses in ~16ms, so the cap stays cheap."
      ]
    }
  ]
}